---
type Props = { city?: string };
const { city } = Astro.props;
const place = city ?? "Georgia";
---

<h2>Questions homeowners ask in {place}</h2>
<dl class="faq">
  <div>
    <dt>How fast does someone come?</dt>
    <dd>
      That depends on the shop, the hour, and how many storms are hitting
      Gwinnett the same night. We cannot promise a 60-minute truck. Emergency
      water is still worth calling now. Drying is cheaper than waiting until
      morning if the house is still taking water.
    </dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt>Can I stay in the house?</dt>
    <dd>
      Often yes on a clean supply-line leak in one room. No if sewage is out,
      the ceiling is coming down, or the panel is wet. The crew on site should
      tell you.
    </dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt>Do I have to hire the company you send?</dt>
    <dd>
      No. Someone will call you. You can get a second opinion before any
      work starts.
    </dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt>What if it is only a small drip?</dt>
    <dd>
      If the water is off and you can see all of it, start on
      <a href="/small-leaks">small leaks</a>. If it still smells or feels damp
      the next day, send the form.
    </dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt>How long does drying take?</dt>
    <dd>
      A one-room clean leak can be a couple of days of fans and a dehumidifier.
      Wet pad, hardwood, or walls often take longer. A shop should measure
      moisture, not guess from how it looks.
    </dd>
  </div>
  <div>
    <dt>Will they work with my insurance?</dt>
    <dd>
      Most restoration companies in this area will. We do not file the claim.
      Photograph first. More on
      <a href="/insurance">insurance</a>.
    </dd>
  </div>
</dl>